Binary Data
You’ve used JSON file formats throughout this book: for meshes, animations, skeletons, text
localization, and now for level loading. The advantages of using a text-based file format are
numerous. Text files are easy for humans to look at, find errors in, and (if needed) manually edit.
Text files also play very nicely with source control systems such as Git because it’s very easy to
see what changed in a file between two revisions. During development, it’s also easier to debug
loading of assets if they are text files.
